{"name":"Gurkha","hex":"#989171","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Gurkha","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of the dominant ethnic group in Nepal, with a Himalayan diaspora.","A member of this people recruited to serve in their own elite units in the British and Indian armies."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Referring or belonging to the Gurkha people.","Referring or belonging to Gurkha soldiers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Gurkha"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gurkha","blocks":[{"text":"The Gurkhas or Gorkhas, with the endonym Gorkhali, are soldiers native to South Asia, chiefly residing within Nepal and some parts of North India."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Nepali_soldiers_Le_Bon_1885.jpg/330px-Nepali_soldiers_Le_Bon_1885.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gurkha","wikidata":"Q207962"},{"title":"Gurkha (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Gurkha is a 2019 Indian Tamil-language action comedy film written and directed by Sam Anton. The film stars Yogi Babu, while Elyssa Erhardt, Anandaraj, Charle, Raj Bharath, and Manobala, among others, play key roles. It revolves around a security officer in a shopping mall who must save hostages after the mall is taken over by terrorists."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/76/Gurkha_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gurkha_(film)","wikidata":"Q65120561"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Gurkha_Soldier_Monument%2C_London_-_April_2008.jpg/500px-Gurkha_Soldier_Monument%2C_London_-_April_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Gurkha_Soldier_Monument%2C_London_-_April_2008.jpg/1280px-Gurkha_Soldier_Monume